    "result_text": "The change is implemented and the full test suite is green (32 tests, 0 failures/errors), including the new `Cp21Tests`.\n\n## What I did\n\nOn successful owner creation, the controller now emits an audit line via the logger named `AUDIT`.\n\nIn `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n- Added a dedicated `AUDIT` logger: `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`.\n- Immediately after `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` in `addOwner(...)`, emit:\n  ```java\n  AUDIT.info(\"owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n      owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n  ```\n\nThe log is emitted after the save, so the persisted owner has its generated `id` and `customerCode`, plus the business-day-adjusted `registrationDate` \u2014 all three appear on the line, which is exactly what `Cp21Tests` asserts via `AuditLogCapture`. Verified line during the run: `AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-08-11`.",
